  "Question": "A housewife saved \\(\\$2.50\\) in buying a dress on sale. If she spent \\(\\$25\\) for the dress, she saved about:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\%\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\%\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The percentage saved compares the saving with the original price. Since she paid \\(\\$25\\) after saving \\(\\$2.50\\), the original price was \\(\\$27.50\\). Thus the percentage saved was\n\\[\n\\frac{2.50}{27.50}\\cdot100\\%\n=\\frac1{11}\\cdot100\\%\n\\approx9.09\\%.\n\\]\nThis is about \\(9\\%\\), choice B.",
